The trusted registry root

The file root.json in this directory is the TUF root metadata that this build of
the CLI trusts as the start of the chain of trust of the plugin registry. It is
embedded in the CLI. Every later root, and every key that signs the index, is
verified against it, so nothing at runtime can add to it or replace it: no
environment variable, config entry or flag.

The root is the first version of the root metadata of the registry. A client
that embeds it walks forward to the current root by itself, so root keys and the
keys of the other roles can be rotated without a new CLI release, as long as
each new root is signed by a threshold of the keys of the root before it.

No production root is embedded yet, see the TODO in ../root.go. Until then every
verification fails with ErrNoTrustedKeys, which is the safe default.
